Role & Context:
implement a Staff Check-in System with 3 main menu features.

Authentication & Setup Requirements:

Create 10 hardcoded staff accounts.

Store the usernames and passwords in the .env file, starting exactly from line 24. (I stored)

Menu 1: Registration Check-in

Inputs: Allow staff to check in students by scanning a QR code, entering a Short Code, or entering a Student ID.

Logic: The underlying functionality must be exactly the same as the "First-Day Check-in" logic.

Menu 2: Registration Statistics & Directory

Overview Metrics: Display the total number of registered students and a breakdown by registration status.

Student List & Search: Display a list of students. Include a search/filter bar to find specific students by First/Last Name, Student ID, or Short Code.

Data Constraints: Only show students who belong to the logged-in staff member's department.

Firebase Optimization (Crucial): Optimize the page for speed and minimize Firebase read queries. Implement pagination or infinite scrolling by fetching and displaying only 5 records at a time (load more upon scrolling).

Menu 3: Walk-in Registration Approval

Logic: Use the existing walkin_approve function.

Backend Behavior: For department allocations, the backend must randomly assign a group to the student and update the database accordingly.

UI Constraint: Do not display the randomly assigned group to the staff member on the frontend.

Success State: Once approved, simply show a success message reading: "Registration successfully approved."

